title: The [+ prime_minister +] cabinet moves to depoliticize the military!
subtitle: A sweeping reshuffle!
view-if: gov_army_timer <= 0 and gov_cooldown_timer <= 0 and year >= 1920 and army_loyalty > 0.71 and king_relation < 5*radicalisation and not national_congress_seen and not prime_minister == "Mussolini" or prime_minister == "D'Annunzio" or prime_minister == "Grandi"
on-arrival: gov_cooldown_timer = 3; gov_army_timer = 6; army_loyalty -= 0.07
new-page: true
tags: event
 
= <span style="color: [+ i_colour +];">[+ king +]</span> depoliticizes the military!

<img src="img/portraits/VitorioEmanuel.jpg" style="float:left; margin-right:1em; margin-bottom:0.5em; width:220px; object-fit:cover; object-position:top; border:2px solid #000000ff;"> Recently, the  [+ prime_minister +] cabinet has begun moving towards a depoliticizing of the military, under the consent of <span style="color: [+ i_colour +];">[+ king +]</span>,  removing several officers and soldiers from positions where they could influence the tide in our favour, that is, <span style="color: [+ psi_colour +];">**socialism**</span>'s favour. They have been reassigned to different spots or mysteriously dismissed, hurting our influence within the army.

Even though the [+ prime_minister +] cabinet might have good intentions,  this naturally allows the more <span style="color: [+ pnf_colour +];">reactionary</span> parts of the military to take more space, with Fasci and Arditi sympathizers increasing within the army. 

- @root: What a hard pill to swallow.

